# The steam module's stores (docs/wrappfile.md#stores), which every stage
# and function of the module sees.
#
# One Steam at a time: two signed in to the same account would knock each
# other off, and both would save the session back when they quit. Every
# Steam app takes this lock while Steam runs, and a build's step while it
# uses the sign-in.
LOCK steam --scope=global
# Two first builds at once don't both lay a client into the one folder.
LOCK client --scope=global
# Steam's client, kept between builds, so Steam needn't update itself each
# time: a cache, as it can always be downloaded again.
STORE client --retention=cache --scope=global --exclusive=client
# The one sign-in every Steam app and build shares, kept until someone signs
# out (docs/steam.md). Only the steam module's own instructions use it at
# build time; it's never part of an app.
STORE sign-in --scope=global --exclusive=steam
